WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.020 --> 00:00:02.730
JEN PERSON: It's
officially week six

00:00:02.730 --> 00:00:04.620
of Google Cloud
Next on air, which

00:00:04.620 --> 00:00:08.290
means we're focusing on data
management and databases.

00:00:08.290 --> 00:00:11.160
I'm Jen Person, and welcome
to "This Week in Cloud,"

00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:14.880
where we're taking a sneak
peek at this week's content.

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:18.150
Week six is all about data
management and databases,

00:00:18.150 --> 00:00:21.030
meaning we're highlighting how
Google's cloud databases are

00:00:21.030 --> 00:00:24.210
simple to use, without
compromising on security,

00:00:24.210 --> 00:00:27.090
liability or open standards.

00:00:27.090 --> 00:00:29.910
We've got sessions on
data migration stories,

00:00:29.910 --> 00:00:33.000
modernization advice, and
integrating everything

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:36.900
from your Cassandra workloads
to your existing SQL server.

00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:39.150
So be sure to check out
the session catalog.

00:00:39.150 --> 00:00:43.590
And don't forget to explore the
demos to see what you can do.

00:00:43.590 --> 00:00:45.570
No matter what your data
solution looks like,

00:00:45.570 --> 00:00:47.440
it needs to be reliable.

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:49.890
You need to be confident your
database service can recover

00:00:49.890 --> 00:00:53.640
from user errors, infrastructure
failures, and full region

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:54.810
outages.

00:00:54.810 --> 00:00:56.790
That's why we're shining
this week's spotlight

00:00:56.790 --> 00:00:59.010
on high availability
and disaster

00:00:59.010 --> 00:01:01.170
recovery with Cloud SQL.

00:01:01.170 --> 00:01:04.110
This talk is packed full
of advice and insight

00:01:04.110 --> 00:01:06.630
on how Cloud SQL
leverages replication

00:01:06.630 --> 00:01:11.520
and automatic health checks
to keep your database online.

00:01:11.520 --> 00:01:13.792
One session on my
own playlist is how

00:01:13.792 --> 00:01:15.000
to choose the right database.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:17.610
Because there are quite
a few options out there,

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:19.290
and the right one
for you depends

00:01:19.290 --> 00:01:21.135
on what you're trying to do.

00:01:21.135 --> 00:01:23.760
This talk will walk you through
the strengths of various Google

00:01:23.760 --> 00:01:26.370
Cloud databases from the
perspective of different use

00:01:26.370 --> 00:01:29.670
cases, from lift and
shift to modernization

00:01:29.670 --> 00:01:32.640
of existing applications
and net new development,

00:01:32.640 --> 00:01:34.770
this talk covers it all.

00:01:34.770 --> 00:01:36.600
Of course, effective
data management

00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:39.390
is about more than storing
and querying your data.

00:01:39.390 --> 00:01:41.640
Those are just the
foundation building systems

00:01:41.640 --> 00:01:44.700
that offer insights to
empower your business.

00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:47.580
This video demo offers
an example of this

00:01:47.580 --> 00:01:51.090
by showing one retailer can
use Cloud Spanner to build

00:01:51.090 --> 00:01:53.850
a real time inventory
management system to support

00:01:53.850 --> 00:01:56.140
their online sales.

00:01:56.140 --> 00:01:58.480
To out these sessions to
your digital playlist,

00:01:58.480 --> 00:01:59.840
check out the link.

00:01:59.840 --> 00:02:02.200
Any ideas or thoughts,
leave us a comment

00:02:02.200 --> 00:02:05.380
or tweet us using the
hashtag #GoogleCloudNext.

00:02:05.380 --> 00:02:08.550
We'll see you in the cloud.

